  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/160ea81093c6e634fbecf786af065f92c29236f9"/></media></figure></para>
<para>For questions 1 – 5, use the following scenario to graph an inequality from a table:</para>
<blockquote>
  <para>Andre is making trail mix with dried fruit and mixed nuts. Dried fruit costs $3 per pound and mixed nuts cost $6 per pound. He wants to spend no more than $54 on the trail mix. The inequality \(y \leq −2x + 18\) represents the number of pounds of dried fruit, \(y\), he can buy for \(x\) pounds of nuts.</para>
</blockquote>
<!--Q#1-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>The related equation \(y = -2x + 18\) represents the boundary line of the inequality. Complete the table of values to find points on the boundary line of the inequality.</para>
    <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
      <thead>
        <row>
          <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
          <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
        </row>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry>0</entry>
        <entry/>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>2</entry>
        <entry/>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>4</entry>
        <entry/>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>6</entry>
        <entry/>
      </row>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
    <thead>
      <row>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
      </row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry>0</entry>
        <entry>18</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>2</entry>
        <entry>14</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>4</entry>
        <entry>10</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>6</entry>
        <entry>6</entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->
<!--Q#2-->
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. Graph the data from your table of values that represents this scenario using the Desmos tool below. </item>
</list>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <!--QUESTION IS OUTSIDE OF INTERACTION DUE TO DESMOS-->
  <para>When you have finished graphing, select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/380534493b88df7a87955c4e3d4c84bb91997ada"/></media></figure></para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->
<!--Q#3-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Is the boundary line for the inequality \(y \leq −2x + 18\) a solid line or a dashed line? Explain how you know.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The line is solid because the inequality \(\leq\) means the points on the line are included as solutions.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Q#4-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Is the point \((0, 0)\) a solution to the inequality?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Yes, \(0 \leq −2(0) + 18\), \(0 \leq 18\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Q#5-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Use the graph from number 2. Enter the inequality \(y \leq −2x + 18\) to represent the data. Notice the shading for the solution region of this inequality.</para>
    <para>When you have finished graphing, select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/d5fd2962509e03697ac49887823e1eef32f14a8d"/></media></figure></para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->
<para>In problems 6–10, use the data from the table to graph the inequality and write an inequality with two variables.</para>
<table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>-2</entry>
      <entry>-5</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>0</entry>
      <entry>-6</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>2</entry>
      <entry>1</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>3</entry>
      <entry>5</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
